{
  "title": "19: Maryam مريم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nكٓهٰيٰعٓصٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nKAAHAAYAAA’AASAA.\nKaf. Ha. Ya. 'Ain. Sad. \nذِكْرُ رَحْمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبْدَهٗ زَكَرِيَّا ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(2)\nZEKRU RAHMATE RABBEKA A’ABDAH ZAKAREEA.\n(This is) a recital of the Mercy of thy Lord to His servant Zakariya. \nاِذْ نَادٰى رَبَّهٗ نِدَآءً خَفِيًّا‏(3)\nIZ NAADAA WAL NEDAAAN KHAFEEA.\nBehold! he cried to his Lord in secret, \nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّىْ وَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّاْسُ شَيْبًا وَّلَمْ اَكُنْۢ بِدُعَآئِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيًّا‏(4)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE WAHANA AL-A’AZMU MINNEE WAASHTAA’ALA AR-RAASU SHAYBAN LAM AAKUN BEDUA’AAEKA RABBE SHAQEEA.\nPraying: “O my Lord! infirm indeed are my bones, and the hair of my head doth glisten with grey: but never am I unblest, O my Lord, in my prayer to Thee! \nوَاِنِّىْ خِفْتُ الْمَوَالِىَ مِنْ وَّرَآءِىْ وَكَانَتِ امْرَاَتِىْ عَاقِرًا فَهَبْ لِىْ مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ وَلِيًّا ۙ‏(5)\nWA INNEE KHEFTU AL-MAWAALEAAA MIN WWARAAEAA KAANATIL AMRAATEAA A’AAQERAN FAHAB LEE MIN LLADUNKA WALIYYANW.\n“Now I fear (what) my relatives (and colleagues) (will do) after me: but my wife is barren: so give me an heir as from Thyself, \nيَّرِثُنِىْ وَيَرِثُ مِنْ اٰلِ يَعْقُوْبَ ۖ  وَاجْعَلْهُ رَبِّ رَضِيًّا‏(6)\nYYARESUNEAA WAYARESU MIN AALE YA’QOOBAL WAAJA’ALHU RABBE RAZEEA.\n“(One that) will (truly) represent me, and represent the posterity of Jacob; and make him, O my Lord! one with whom Thou art well-pleased!” \nيٰزَكَرِيَّاۤ اِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلٰم اۨسْمُهٗ يَحْيٰى ۙ لَمْ نَجْعَلْ لَّهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُ سَمِيًّا‏(7)\nYAAZAKAREEA INNAA NUBASSHERUKA BEGHULAAM FEEHAS YAHYAA LAM NAJ-A’L LAHU MIN QABLO SAMEEA.\n(His prayer was answered): “O Zakariya! We give thee good news of a son: His name shall be Yahya: on none by that name have We conferred distinction before.” \nقَالَ رَبِّ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لِىْ غُلٰمٌ وَّكَانَتِ امْرَاَتِىْ عَاقِرًا وَّقَدْ بَلَغْتُ مِنَ الْكِبَرِ عِتِيًّا‏(8)\nQAALA RABBE ANNAA LAHUL LEE GHULAAMUN WWAKAANATE AMRAATEAA A’AAQERAN WWAQAD BALAGHTU MENAL AL-KEBARE E’ETEEA.\nHe said: “O my Lord! How shall I have a son, when my wife is barren and I have grown quite decrepit from old age?” \nقَالَ كَذٰلِكَ‌ۚ قَالَ رَبُّكَ هُوَ عَلَىَّ هَيِّنٌ وَّقَدْ خَلَقْتُكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلَمْ تَكُ شَيْئًا‏(9)\nQAALA KAZAALEKA QAALA RABBOKA HOWA A’LAYYA HAYNUN WWAQAD KHALAQTUKA MIN QABLO WA LAM TAKU SHAY-ANW.\nHe said: “So (it will be) thy Lord saith, 'that is easy for Me: I did indeed create thee before, when thou hadst been nothing!'“ \nقَالَ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ لِّىْۤ اٰيَةً‌  ؕ قَالَ اٰيَتُكَ اَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلٰثَ لَيَالٍ سَوِيًّا‏(10)\nQAALA RABBE A’L LEE AAYATAL QAALA AAAYATUKA ALLAA TUKALLEMA NAASA SALAASA LAYAALIN SAWIYYAN.\n(Zakariya) said: “O my Lord! give me a Sign.” “Thy Sign,” was the answer, “Shall be that thou shalt speak to no man for three nights, although thou art not dumb.” \nفَخَرَجَ عَلٰى قَوْمِهٖ مِنَ الْمِحْرَابِ فَاَوْحٰٓى اِلَيْهِمْ اَنْ سَبِّحُوْا بُكْرَةً وَّعَشِيًّا‏(11)\nFAKHARAJA A’LAA QAWMEHI MENAL AL-MEHRAABE FAAWHAAA ELAYHIM AN SABBEHOOA BUKRATANW WWAA’ASHEEA.\nSo Zakariya came out to his people from him chamber: He told them by signs to celebrate Allah's praises in the morning and in the evening. \nيٰيَحْيٰى خُذِ الْكِتٰبَ بِقُوَّةٍ‌ ؕ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ الْحُكْمَ صَبِيًّا ۙ‏(12)\nYAAYAHYAA KHUZE KETAABA BE-QUWWATINW WA AATAYNAAHO AL-HUKMA SABEEA.\n(To his son came the command): “O Yahya! take hold of the Book with might”: and We gave him Wisdom even as a youth, \nوَّحَنَانًا مِّنْ لَّدُنَّا وَزَكٰوةً  ‌ؕ وَّكَانَ تَقِيًّا ۙ‏(13)\nWWAHANAANAN MIN WA WAZAKAAWTAN WA KAANA TAQEEA.\nAnd piety (for all creatures) as from Us, and purity: He was devout, \nوَّبَرًّۢا بِوَالِدَيْهِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ جَبَّارًا عَصِيًّا‏(14)\nWWABARRAN INSAANA WA LAM YAKUL JABBAARAN A’ASEEA.\nAnd kind to his parents, and he was not overbearing or rebellious. \nوَسَلٰمٌ عَلَيْهِ يَوْمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوْمَ يَمُوْتُ وَيَوْمَ يُبْعَثُ حَيًّا‏(15)\nWA SALAAMUN A’LAYHE YAWMA WULEDA WA YAWMA YAMOOTO WA YAWMA YUBA’ASU HAYYANW.\nSo Peace on him the day he was born, the day that he dies, and the day that he will be raised up to life (again)! \nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مَرْيَمَ‌ۘ اِذِ انْتَبَذَتْ مِنْ اَهْلِهَا مَكَانًا شَرْقِيًّا ۙ‏(16)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE MARYAMAL EZIM ANTABAZAT MIN AHLEHAA MAKAANAN SHARQEEA.\nRelate in the Book (the story of) Mary, when she withdrew from her family to a place in the East. \nفَاتَّخَذَتْ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمْ حِجَابًا فَاَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهَا رُوْحَنَا فَتَمَثَّلَ لَهَا بَشَرًا سَوِيًّا‏(17)\nFAATTAKHAZAT MIN DOONEHEM HEJAABAN FA-ARSALNAA ELAYHAA ROOHANAA FATAMASSALA LAHAA BASHARAN SAWIYYAN.\nShe placed a screen (to screen herself) from them; then We sent her our angel, and he appeared before her as a man in all respects. \nقَالَتْ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِالرَّحْمٰنِ مِنْكَ اِنْ كُنْتَ تَقِيًّا‏(18)\nQAALAT INNEE A-OO’ZO BE-RAHMAANIR MENKA IN KUNTA TAQEEA.\nShe said: “I seek refuge from thee to (Allah) Most Gracious: (come not near) if thou dost fear Allah.” \n‌قَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا رَسُوْلُ رَبِّكِ ‌ ۖ  لِاَهَبَ لَكِ غُلٰمًا زَكِيًّا‏(19)\nQAALA INNAMAA ANAA RASOOLAL RABBEKE LEAAHABA LAKE GHULAAMAN ZAKEEA.\nHe said: “Nay, I am only a messenger from thy Lord, (to announce) to thee the gift of a holy son. \nقَالَتْ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لِىْ غُلٰمٌ وَّلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِىْ بَشَرٌ وَّلَمْ اَكُ بَغِيًّا‏(20)\nQAALAT ANNAA LAHUL LEE GHULAAMUN LAM YAMSASNEAA BASHARUM LAM AAKU BAGHEEA.\nShe said: “How shall I have a son, seeing that no man has touched me, and I am not unchaste?” \nقَالَ كَذٰلِكِ‌ ۚ قَالَ رَبُّكِ هُوَ عَلَىَّ هَيِّنٌ‌ ۚ وَلِنَجْعَلَهٗۤ اٰيَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَرَحْمَةً مِّنَّا‌ ۚ وَكَانَ اَمْرًا مَّقْضِيًّا‏(21)\nQAALA KAZAALEKE QAALA RABBUKE HOWA A’LAYYA HAYNUN WALENAJA’ALAH AAYATAL LIN-NAASE WA RAHMATAM MINNAA KAANAL AMRAN MMAQZEEA.\nHe said: “So (it will be): Thy Lord saith, 'that is easy for Me: and (We wish) to appoint him as a Sign unto men and a Mercy from Us':It is a matter (so) decreed.” \nفَحَمَلَتْهُ فَانْتَبَذَتْ بِهٖ مَكَانًا قَصِيًّا‏(22)\nFA-HAMALATHO FANTABAZAT BEHI MAKAANAN QASIYYAA.\nSo she conceived him, and she retired with him to a remote place. \nفَاَجَآءَهَا الْمَخَاضُ اِلٰى جِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ‌ۚ قَالَتْ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ مِتُّ قَبْلَ هٰذَا وَكُنْتُ نَسْيًا مَّنْسِيًّا‏(23)\nFA-AJAAA-AHAL MAKHAAZO ELAA JIZ-I’N NAKHLAH, QAALAT YAA LAYTANEE MITTO QABLA HAAZAA WA KUNTO NASYAM MANSIYYAA.\nAnd the pains of childbirth drove her to the trunk of a palm-tree: She cried (in her anguish): “Ah! would that I had died before this! would that I had been a thing forgotten and out of sight!” \nفَنَادٰٮهَا مِنْ تَحْتِهَاۤ اَلَّا تَحْزَنِىْ قَدْ جَعَلَ رَبُّكِ تَحْتَكِ سَرِيًّا‏(24)\nFA-NAADAAHAA MIN TAHTEHAA ALLAA TAHZANEE QAD JA-A’LA RABBOKE TAHTAKE SARIYYAA.\nBut (a voice) cried to her from beneath the (palm-tree): “Grieve not! for thy Lord hath provided a rivulet beneath thee; \nوَهُزِّىْۤ اِلَيْكِ بِجِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ تُسٰقِطْ عَلَيْكِ رُطَبًا جَنِيًّا‏(25)\nWA HUZZEE ELAYKE BE-JIZ-I’N NAKHLATE TOSAAQIT A’LAYKE ROTABAN JANIYYAA.\n“And shake towards thyself the trunk of the palm-tree: It will let fall fresh ripe dates upon thee. \nفَكُلِىْ وَاشْرَبِىْ وَقَرِّىْ عَيْنًا‌ ۚ فَاِمَّا تَرَيِنَّ مِنَ الْبَشَرِ اَحَدًا ۙ فَقُوْلِىْۤ اِنِّىْ نَذَرْتُ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ صَوْمًا فَلَنْ اُكَلِّمَ الْيَوْمَ اِنْسِيًّا ‌ۚ‏(26)\nFA-KOLEE WASHRABEE WA QARREE A’YNAA, FA-IMMAA TARAYINNA MENAL BASHARE AHADAN, FA-QOOLEE INNEE NAZARTO LIR-RAHMAANE SAWMAA FA-LAN OKALLEMAL YAWMA INSIYYAA.\n“So eat and drink and cool (thine) eye. And if thou dost see any man, say, 'I have vowed a fast to (Allah) Most Gracious, and this day will I enter into not talk with any human being'“ \nفَاَتَتْ بِهٖ قَوْمَهَا تَحْمِلُهٗ‌ؕ قَالُوْا يٰمَرْيَمُ لَقَدْ جِئْتِ شَيْئًا فَرِيًّا‏(27)\nFA-ATAT BEHI QAWMAHAA TAHMELOH, QAALOO YAA MARYAMO LAQAD JEATE SHAY-AN FARIYYAA.\nAt length she brought the (babe) to her people, carrying him (in her arms). They said: “O Mary! truly an amazing thing hast thou brought! \nيٰۤاُخْتَ هٰرُوْنَ مَا كَانَ اَ بُوْكِ امْرَاَ سَوْءٍ وَّمَا كَانَتْ اُمُّكِ بَغِيًّا‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(28)\nYAA UKHTA HAAROONA MAA KAANA ABOOKIM RA-A SAWINW WA MAA KAANAT UMMOKE BAGHIYYAA.\n“O sister of Aaron! Thy father was not a man of evil, nor thy mother a woman unchaste!” \nفَاَشَارَتْ اِلَيْهِ‌ ؕ قَالُوْا كَيْفَ نُكَلِّمُ مَنْ كَانَ فِى الْمَهْدِ صَبِيًّا‏(29)\nFA-ASHAARAT ELAYH, QAALOO KAYFA NOKALLEMO MAN KAANA FIL MAHDE SABIYYAA.\nBut she pointed to the babe. They said: “How can we talk to one who is a child in the cradle?” \nقَالَ اِنِّىْ عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ ؕ اٰتٰٮنِىَ الْكِتٰبَ وَجَعَلَنِىْ نَبِيًّا ۙ‏(30)\nQAALA INNEE A’BDUL LAAH, AATAANEYAL KETAABA WA JA-A’LANEE NABIYYANW.\nHe said: “I am indeed a servant of Allah: He hath given me revelation and made me a prophet; \nوَّجَعَلَنِىْ مُبٰرَكًا اَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُ وَاَوْصٰنِىْ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَالزَّكٰوةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا ‌ۖ ‏(31)\nWA JA-A’LANEE MOBAARAKAN AYNA MAA KUNT, WA AWSAANEE BIS-SALAATE WAZ ZAKAATE MAA DUMTO HAYYANW.\n“And He hath made me blessed wheresoever I be, and hath enjoined on me Prayer and Charity as long as I live; \nوَّبَرًّۢابِوَالِدَتِىْ وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْنِىْ جَبَّارًا شَقِيًّا‏(32)\nWA BARRAM BE-WAALEDATEE, WA LAM YAJ-A’LNEE JABBAARAN SHAQIYYAA.\n“(He) hath made me kind to my mother, and not overbearing or miserable; \nوَالسَّلٰمُ عَلَىَّ يَوْمَ وُلِدْتُّ وَيَوْمَ اَمُوْتُ وَيَوْمَ اُبْعَثُ حَيًّا‏(33)\nWAS SALAAMO A’LAYYA YAWMA WOLIDTO WA YAWMA AMOOTO WA YAWMA UB-A’SO HAYYAA.\n“So peace is on me the day I was born, the day that I die, and the day that I shall be raised up to life (again)”! \nذٰ لِكَ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ‌ۚ قَوْلَ الْحَقِّ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ يَمْتَرُوْنَ‏(34)\nZAALEKA E’ESAB NO MARYAM, QAWLAL HAQQIL LAZEE FEEHE YAMTAROON.\nSuch (was) Jesus the son of Mary: (it is) a statement of truth, about which they (vainly) dispute. \nمَا كَانَ لِلّٰهِ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ مِنْ وَّلَدٍ‌ۙ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ؕ اِذَا قَضٰٓى اَمْرًا فَاِنَّمَا يَقُوْلُ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُؕ‏(35)\nMAA KAANA LILLAAHE ANY YATTAKHEZA MINW WALADIN, SUBHAANAH, EZAA QAZAA AMRAN FA-INNAMAA YAQOOLO LAHU KUN FA-YAKOON.\nIt is not befitting to (the majesty of) Allah that He should beget a son. Glory be to Him! when He determines a matter, He only says to it, “Be”, and it is. \nوَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْهُ ‌ؕ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(36)\nWA INNAL LAAHA RABBEE WA RABBOKUM FA’BODOOH, HAAZAA SERAATUM MUSTAQEEM.\nVerily Allah is my Lord and your Lord: Him therefore serve ye: this is a Way that is straight. \nفَاخْتَلَفَ الْاَحْزَابُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِهِمْ‌ۚ فَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ مَّشْهَدِ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(37)\nFAKHTALAFAL AHZAABO MIM BAYNEHIM, FA-WAYLUL LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO MIM MASH-HADE YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nBut the sects differ among themselves: and woe to the unbelievers because of the (coming) Judgment of a Momentous Day! \nاَسْمِعْ بِهِمْ وَاَبْصِرْۙ يَوْمَ يَاْتُوْنَنَا‌ لٰكِنِ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ الْيَوْمَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(38)\nAASMEA’ BEHIM WAABSER YAWMA YAATOONANAA LAAKENE ZAALEMOON YAWMA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nHow plainly will they see and hear, the Day that they will appear before Us! but the unjust today are in error manifest! \nوَاَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْحَسْرَةِ اِذْ قُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ‌‌ۘ وَهُمْ فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ وَّهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(39)\nWAANZERHUM YAWMA AL-HASRATE IZ QUZEAAA MIN WA HUM FEE GHAFLATIM WA HUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nBut warn them of the Day of Distress, when the matter will be determined: for (behold,) they are negligent and they do not believe! \nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نَرِثُ الْاَرْضَ وَمَنْ عَلَيْهَا وَاِلَيْنَا يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(40)\nINNAA NAHNO NARESU ARZA WA MAN A’LAYHAA WA ELAYNAA YARJEO’ON.\nIt is We Who will inherit the earth, and all beings thereon: to Us will they all be returned. \nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ ۙ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صِدِّيْقًا نَّبِيًّا‏(41)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE IBRAAHEEMA INNAHU KAANA SEDDEEQAN NNABEEA.\n(Also mention in the Book (the story of) Abraham: He was a man of Truth, a prophet. \nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ يٰۤاَبَتِ لِمَ تَعْبُدُ مَا لَا يَسْمَعُ وَلَا يُبْصِرُ وَ لَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْكَ شَيْئًا‏(42)\nIZ QAALA LEAABEEHE YAA LEMA TAA’BUDU MAA LAA YASMA-O’ WA LAA YUBSERU WA LAA YUGHNEE A’NKAL SHAY-ANW.\nBehold, he said to his father: “O my father! why worship that which heareth not and seeth not, and can profit thee nothing? \nيٰۤاَبَتِ اِنِّىْ قَدْ جَآءَنِىْ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ مَا لَمْ يَاْتِكَ فَاتَّبِعْنِىْۤ اَهْدِكَ صِرَاطًا سَوِيًّا‏(43)\nYAA INNEE QAD JAAANEAA MENAL I’LME MAA LAM YAATEKA FAATTABEA’NEAA AAHDEKA SERAATAM SAWIYYAN.\n“O my father! to me hath come knowledge which hath not reached thee: so follow me: I will guide thee to a way that is even and straight. \nيٰۤاَبَتِ لَا تَعْبُدِ الشَّيْطٰنَ‌ ؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ كَانَ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ عَصِيًّا‏(44)\nYAA LAA TAA’BUDE ASH-SHAYTAANA INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA KAANA LELRRAHMAANE A’ASEEA.\n“O my father! serve not Satan: for Satan is a rebel against (Allah) Most Gracious. \nيٰۤاَبَتِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يَّمَسَّكَ عَذَابٌ مِّنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ فَتَكُوْنَ لِلشَّيْطٰنِ وَلِيًّا‏(45)\nYAA INNEE AKHAAFO AN YYAMASSAKA A’ZAABUN MENAL RAHMAANIR FA TAKOONA LELSSHAYTAANE WALIYYANW.\n“O my father! I fear lest a Penalty afflict thee from (Allah) Most Gracious, so that thou become to Satan a friend.” \nقَالَ اَرَاغِبٌ اَنْتَ عَنْ اٰلِهَتِىْ يٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُ‌ۚ لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ لَاَرْجُمَنَّكَ‌ وَاهْجُرْنِىْ مَلِيًّا‏(46)\nQAALA AARAAGHEBUN ANTA A’N AAALEHATEAA YAABRAAHEEMU LAIL LAM TANTAHE LAARJUMANNAKA WAAHJURNEAA MALEEA.\n(The father) replied: “Dost thou hate my gods, O Abraham? If thou forbear not, I will indeed stone thee: Now get away from me for a good long while!” \nقَالَ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكَ‌ۚ سَاَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكَ رَبِّىْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِىْ حَفِيًّا‏(47)\nQAALA SALAAMUN A’LAYKA SAASTAGHFERU LAKA RABBEAA INNAHU KAANA BEE HAFEEA.\nAbraham said: “Peace be on thee: I will pray to my Lord for thy forgiveness: for He is to me Most Gracious. \nوَ اَعْتَزِلُكُمْ وَمَا تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَاَدْعُوْا رَبِّىْ‌ ‌ۖ  عَسٰٓى اَلَّاۤ اَكُوْنَ بِدُعَآءِ رَبِّىْ شَقِيًّا‏(48)\nWA AAA’TAZELUKUM WA MAA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WAADU’OOA RABBEE A’SAA ALLAA SHAY-IWN WA BE-DO-A’AA-IL RABBEE SHAQEEA.\n“And I will turn away from you (all) and from those whom ye invoke besides Allah: I will call on my Lord: perhaps, by my prayer to my Lord, I shall be not unblest.” \nفَلَمَّا اعْتَزَلَهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ۙ وَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ‌ ؕ وَكُلًّا جَعَلْنَا نَبِيًّا‏(49)\nFALAMMAA AA’TAZALAHUM WA MAA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE WAHABNAA LAHU ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WAKULLAN JA-A’LNAA NABEEA.\nWhen he had turned away from them and from those whom they worshipped besides Allah, We bestowed on him Isaac and Jacob, and each one of them We made a prophet. \nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّحْمَتِنَا وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ عَلِيًّا‏(50)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHUM MIN RRAHMATENAA WA JA-A’LNAA LAHUM LESAANA SEDQIN A’ALEEA.\nAnd We bestowed of Our Mercy on them, and We granted them lofty honour on the tongue of truth. \nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مُوْسٰٓى‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مُخْلَصًا وَّكَانَ رَسُوْلًا نَّبِيًّا‏(51)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE MOOSAA INNAHU KAANA MUKHLASAN WA KAANA RASOOLAM NNABEEA.\nAlso mention in the Book (the story of) Moses: for he was specially chosen, and he was a messenger (and) a prophet. \nوَنَادَيْنٰهُ مِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ الْاَيْمَنِ وَقَرَّبْنٰهُ نَجِيًّا‏(52)\nWANAADAYNAAHU MIN JAANEBIT TOORE AYMANE WAQARRABNAAHU NAJEEA.\nAnd we called him from the right side of Mount (Sinai), and made him draw near to Us, for mystic (converse). \nوَ وَهَبْنَا لَهٗ مِنْ رَّحْمَتِنَاۤ اَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ نَبِيًّا‏(53)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU MIN RRAHMATENAA AAKHAAHU AALO NABEEA.\nAnd, out of Our Mercy, We gave him his brother Aaron, (also) a prophet. \nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِسْمٰعِيْلَ‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صَادِقَ الْوَعْدِ وَكَانَ رَسُوْلًا نَّبِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(54)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE AESMAAE’EELA INNAHU KAANA SAADEQA AL-WAA’DE KAANAL RASOOLAM NNABEEA.\nAlso mention in the Book (the story of) Isma'il: He was (strictly) true to what he promised, and he was a messenger (and) a prophet. \nوَ كَانَ يَاْمُرُ اَهْلَهٗ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَالزَّكٰوةِ وَكَانَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ مَرْضِيًّا‏(55)\nWA KAANA YAAMURU AHLAHU BEALSSALAAWTE WAALZZAKAAWTE KAANAL I’NDAL RABBEHI MARZEEA.\nHe used to enjoin on his people Prayer and Charity, and he was most acceptable in the sight of his Lord. \nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِدْرِيْسَ‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صِدِّيْقًا نَّبِيًّا ۙ ‏(56)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE AEDREESA INNAHU KAANA SEDDEEQAN NNABEEA.\nAlso mention in the Book the case of Idris: He was a man of truth (and sincerity), (and) a prophet: \nوَّرَفَعْنٰهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا‏(57)\nWWARAFAA’NAAHU MAKAANAN A’ALEEA.\nAnd We raised him to a lofty station. \nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ النَّبِيّٖنَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ اٰدَمَ وَمِمَّنْ حَمَلْنَا مَعَ نُوْحٍ وَّمِنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَمِمَّنْ هَدَيْنَا وَاجْتَبَيْنَا‌ ؕ اِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُ الرَّحْمٰنِ خَرُّوْا سُجَّدًا وَّبُكِيًّا ۩‏(58)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA AN-A’MAL LAAHO A’LAYHIM MENAL NABIYYEENA MIN ZURREETE AADAMAL WA MIMMAN HAMALNAA LAAHA NOOHIN WA MIN ZURREETE IBRAAHEEMA WA ISRAAA-EELAZ WA MIMMAN HADAYNAA WAAJTABAYNAA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATUL RAHMAANIR KHARROOA SUJJADANW WWABUKEEA.\nThose were some of the prophets on whom Allah did bestow His Grace, of the posterity of Adam, and of those who We carried (in the Ark) with Noah, and of the posterity of Abraham and Israel of those whom We guided and chose. Whenever the Signs of (Allah) Most Gracious were rehearsed to them, they would fall down in prostrate adoration and in tears. [۩] \nفَخَلَفَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ اَضَاعُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاتَّبَعُوا الشَّهَوٰتِ‌ فَسَوْفَ يَلْقَوْنَ غَيًّا ۙ‏(59)\nFAKHALAFA MIN BA’DEHIM KHALFUN AAZAAU’OOA SALAATA WAATTABAU’OOA ASH-SHAHAWTE FA-SAWFA YALQAWNA GHAYA.\nBut after them there followed a posterity who missed prayers and followed after lusts soon, then, will they face Destruction, \nاِلَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ شَيْئًا ۙ‏(60)\nILLAA MAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YADKHOLOONA JANNATA WA LAA LAA YUZLAMOON SHAY-ANW.\nExcept those who repent and believe, and work righteousness: for these will enter the Garden and will not be wronged in the least, \nجَنّٰتِ عَدْنٍ اۨلَّتِىْ وَعَدَ الرَّحْمٰنُ عِبَادَهٗ بِالْغَيْبِ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ وَعْدُهٗ مَاْتِيًّا‏(61)\nJANNATIN A’ADNIN LATEE WA-A’DAR RAHMAANO E’EBAADAH BIL-GHAYBE INNAHU KAANA WA’DOHU MAATEEA.\nGardens of Eternity, those which (Allah) Most Gracious has promised to His servants in the Unseen: for His promise must (necessarily) come to pass. \nلَّا يَسْمَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا لَغْوًا اِلَّا سَلٰمًا‌ؕ وَلَهُمْ رِزْقُهُمْ فِيْهَا بُكْرَةً وَّعَشِيًّا‏(62)\nLAA YAS-MA-O’ONA FEEHAA LAGHWANW ILLAA SALAAMAN WA LAHUM REZQUHUM FEEHAA BUKRATANW WWAA’ASHEEA.\nThey will not there hear any vain discourse, but only salutations of Peace: And they will have therein their sustenance, morning and evening. \nتِلْكَ الْجَنَّةُ الَّتِىْ نُوْرِثُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا مَنْ كَانَ تَقِيًّا‏(63)\nTILKA JANNATO LATEE NOORESU MIN E’EBAADENAA MAN KAANA TAQEEA.\nSuch is the Garden which We give as an inheritance to those of Our servants who guard against Evil. \nوَمَا نَتَنَزَّلُ اِلَّا بِاَمْرِ رَبِّكَ‌ ۚ لَهٗ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْنَا وَمَا خَلْفَنَا وَمَا بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ‌ ۚ وَمَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ نَسِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(64)\nWA MAA NATANAZZALU ILLAA BE-AMRE RABBEKA LAHU MAA BAYNA AYDEENAA WA MAA KHALFANAA WA MAA BAYNA ZAA LEKA WA MAA KAANA RABBOKA NASEEA.\n(The angels say:) “We descend not but by command of thy Lord: to Him belongeth what is before us and what is behind us, and what is between: and thy Lord never doth forget, \nرَّبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فَاعْبُدْهُ وَاصْطَبِرْ لِعِبَادَتِهٖ‌ؕ هَلْ تَعْلَمُ لَهٗ سَمِيًّا‏(65)\nRRABBU SAMAAWAATE WA ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FAAA’BUDHU WAASTABER LEE’EBAADATEH HAL TAA’LAMU LAHU SAMEEA.\n“Lord of the heavens and of the earth, and of all that is between them; so worship Him, and be constant and patient in His worship: knowest thou of any who is worthy of the same Name as He?” \nوَيَقُوْلُ الْاِنْسَانُ ءَاِذَا مَا مِتُّ لَسَوْفَ اُخْرَجُ حَيًّا‏(66)\nWA YAQOOLO INSAANO A-EZAA MAA METTU LASAWFA AUKHRAJU HAYYANW.\nMan says: “What! When I am dead, shall I then be raised up alive?” \nاَوَلَا يَذْكُرُ الْاِنْسَانُ اَنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلَمْ يَكُ شَيْئًا‏(67)\nAWA LAA YAZKURU INSAANO ANNAA KHALAQNAAHO MIN QABLO WA LAM YAKU SHAY-ANW.\nBut does not man call to mind that We created him before out of nothing? \nفَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَحْشُرَنَّهُمْ وَالشَّيٰطِيْنَ ثُمَّ لَنُحْضِرَنَّهُمْ حَوْلَ جَهَنَّمَ جِثِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(68)\nFAWARABBEKA LANAHSHURANNAHUM WA SHAYAATEENA SUMMA LANUHZERANNAHUM HAWLA JAHANNAMA JESEEA.\nSo, by thy Lord, without doubt, We shall gather them together, and (also) the Evil Ones (with them); then shall We bring them forth on their knees round about Hell; \nثُمَّ لَنَنْزِعَنَّ مِنْ كُلِّ شِيْعَةٍ اَيُّهُمْ اَشَدُّ عَلَى الرَّحْمٰنِ عِتِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(69)\nSUMMA LANANZEA’ANNA MIN KULLE SHEEA’ATIN AAYHUM ASHADDO A’LAL RAHMAANIR E’ETEEA.\nThen shall We certainly drag out from every sect all those who were worst in obstinate rebellion against (Allah) Most Gracious. \nثُمَّ لَنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ اَوْلٰى بِهَا صِلِيًّا‏(70)\nSUMMA LANAHNU A-A’LAMO BE-LAZEENA HUM AAWLAA BEHAA SELEEA.\nAnd certainly We know best those who are most worthy of being burned therein. \nوَاِنْ مِّنْکُمْ اِلَّا وَارِدُهَا ‌ؕ كَانَ عَلٰى رَبِّكَ حَتْمًا مَّقْضِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(71)\nWA MENM ILLAA WAAREDUHAA KAANA A’LAA RABBEKA HATMAN MMAQZEEA.\nNot one of you but will pass over it: this is, with thy Lord, a Decree which must be accomplished. \nثُمَّ نُنَجِّى الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا وَّنَذَرُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ فِيْهَا جِثِيًّا‏(72)\nSUMMA NUNAJJEAA LAZEENA TAQAW WWANAZARU ZAALEMEEN FEEHAA JESEEA.\nBut We shall save those who guarded against evil, and We shall leave the wrong-doers therein, (humbled) to their knees. \nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا ۙ اَىُّ الْفَرِيْقَيْنِ خَيْرٌ مَّقَامًا وَّاَحْسَنُ نَدِيًّا‏(73)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LILLAZEENA AAMANOO AAA AL-FAREEQAYNE KHAYRUL MMAQAAMAN WWAAHSANU NADEEA.\nWhen Our Clear Signs are rehearsed to them, the Unbelievers say to those who believe, “Which of the two sides is best in point of position? Which makes the best show in council?” \nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ هُمْ اَحْسَنُ اَثَاثًا وَّرِءْيًا‏(74)\nWA AHLAKNAL QABLAHUM MIN QARNIN HUM AHSANO AASAASAN WWAREYAN.\nBut how many (countless) generations before them have we destroyed, who were even better in equipment and in glitter to the eye? \nقُلْ مَنْ كَانَ فِى الضَّلٰلَةِ فَلْيَمْدُدْ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ مَدًّا ۚ‌ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا رَاَوْا مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَ اِمَّا الْعَذَابَ وَاِمَّا السَّاعَةَ ؕ فَسَيَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ هُوَ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا وَّاَضْعَفُ جُنْدًا‏(75)\nQUL MAN KAANA FIL AZ-ZALAALATE FALYAMDUD LAHUL RAHMAANO MADDAN HATTAA EZAA RA-AW MAA YOOA’ADOONA IMMAA A’ZAABA WA AMMAA SAA-A’TA FA SA-YA’LAMOONA MAN HOWA HOWA MMAKAANAN WWAAZA’AFU JUNDAN.\nSay: “If any men go astray, (Allah) Most Gracious extends (the rope) to them, until, when they see the warning of Allah (being fulfilled) - either in punishment or in (the approach of) the Hour, they will at length realise who is worst in position, and (who) weakest in forces! \nوَيَزِيْدُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اهْتَدَوْا هُدًى‌ؕ وَالْبٰقِيٰتُ الصّٰلِحٰتُ خَيْرٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ ثَوَابًا وَّخَيْرٌ مَّرَدًّا‏(76)\nWAYAZEEDU LAAHO LAZEENA TADAW HUDAN WAL BAAQEETU AS-SAALEHAATU KHAYRUL I’NDAL RABBEKA SAWAABAN WWAKHAYRUN MMARADDAN.\n“And Allah doth advance in guidance those who seek guidance: and the things that endure, Good Deeds, are best in the sight of thy Lord, as rewards, and best in respect of (their) eventual return.” \nاَفَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ كَفَرَ بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَقَالَ لَاُوْتَيَنَّ مَالًا وَّوَلَدًا ؕ‏(77)\nAAFARAAYTA LAZEE KAFARA BE-AAYAATENAA WA QAALA LAAWTAYANNA MAALAWN WWAWALADAN.\nHast thou then seen the (sort of) man who rejects Our Signs, yet says: “I shall certainly be given wealth and children?” \nاَطَّلَعَ الْغَيْبَ اَمِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمٰنِ عَهْدًا ۙ‏(78)\nAATTALAA’A GHAYBA AMIL TAKHAZA I’NDAL RAHMAANIR A’HDAN.\nHas he penetrated to the Unseen, or has he taken a contract with (Allah) Most Gracious? \nكَلَّا ‌ ؕ سَنَكْتُبُ مَا يَقُوْلُ وَنَمُدُّ لَهٗ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ مَدًّا ۙ‏(79)\nKALLAA SANAKTUBU MAA YAQOOLO WANAMUDDU LAHU MENAL A’ZAABE MADDAN.\nNay! We shall record what he says, and We shall add and add to his punishment. \nوَّنَرِثُهٗ مَا يَقُوْلُ وَيَاْتِيْنَا فَرْدًا‏(80)\nWWANARESUH MAA YAQOOLO WAYAATEENAA FARDAN.\nTo Us shall return all that he talks of and he shall appear before Us bare and alone. \nوَاتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اٰلِهَةً لِّيَكُوْنُوْا لَهُمْ عِزًّا ۙ‏(81)\nWAT-TAKHAZOO MIN DOONIL LAAHE AALEHATAL LLEEKOONOOA LAHUM E’EZZAN.\nAnd they have taken (for worship) gods other than Allah, to give them power and glory! \nكَلَّا‌ ؕ سَيَكْفُرُوْنَ بِعِبَادَتِهِمْ وَيَكُوْنُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضِدًّا‏(82)\nKALLAA SA-YAKFOROON BEE’EBAADATEHEM WAYAKOONOONA A’LAYHIM ZEDDAN.\nInstead, they shall reject their worship, and become adversaries against them. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا الشَّيٰطِيْنَ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ تَؤُزُّهُمْ اَزًّا ۙ‏(83)\nALAM TARA ANNAA ARSALNAA SHAYAATEENA A’LAL KAAFEREEN TAUZZUHUM AAZZAN.\nSeest thou not that We have set the Evil Ones on against the unbelievers, to incite them with fury? \nفَلَا تَعْجَلْ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا نَعُدُّ لَهُمْ عَدًّا‌ ۚ‏(84)\nFALAA TAA’JAL A’LAYHIM INNAMAA NAU’UDDU LAHUM A’ADDAN.\nSo make no haste against them, for We but count out to them a (limited) number (of days). \nيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ اِلَى الرَّحْمٰنِ وَفْدًا‌ ۙ‏(85)\nYAWMA NAHSHORO MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN ELAL RAHMAANIR WAFDAN.\nThe day We shall gather the righteous to (Allah) Most Gracious, like a band presented before a king for honours, \nوَّنَسُوْقُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَ وِرْدًا‌ ۘ‏(86)\nWWANASOOQU MUJREMEEN ELAA JAHANNAMA WERDAN.\nAnd We shall drive the sinners to Hell, like thirsty cattle driven down to water, \nلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ الشَّفَاعَةَ اِلَّا مَنِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمٰنِ عَهْدًا‌ ۘ‏(87)\nLAA YAMLEKOONA ASH-SHAFAAA’ATA ILLAA MANIS TAKHAZA I’NDAL RAHMAANIR A’HDAN.\nNone shall have the power of intercession, but such a one as has received permission (or promise) from (Allah) Most Gracious. \nوَقَالُوْا اتَّخَذَ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَلَدًا ؕ‏(88)\nWA QAALOO TAKHAZA RAHMAANO LAAHO.\nThey say: “(Allah) Most Gracious has begotten a son!” \nلَقَدْ جِئْتُمْ شَيْئًا اِدًّا ۙ‏(89)\nLAQAD JETUM SHAY-ANW AEDDAN.\nIndeed ye have put forth a thing most monstrous! \nتَكَادُ السَّمٰوٰتُ يَتَفَطَّرْنَ مِنْهُ وَتَنْشَقُّ الْاَرْضُ وَتَخِرُّ الْجِبَالُ هَدًّا ۙ‏(90)\nTAKAADO AS-SAMAAWAATU YATAFATTARNA MINHO WATANSHAQQU ARZO WATAKHERRU JEBAALO HADDAN.\nAt it the skies are ready to burst, the earth to split asunder, and the mountains to fall down in utter ruin, \nاَنْ دَعَوْا لِلرَّحْمٰنِ وَلَدًا‌ ۚ‏(91)\nAN DA-A’W LELRRAHMAANE LAAHO.\nThat they should invoke a son for (Allah) Most Gracious. \nوَمَا يَنْۢبَغِىْ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ وَلَدًا ؕ‏(92)\nWA MAA LAHAA LELRRAHMAANE AN YYATTAKHEZA LAAHO.\nFor it is not consonant with the majesty of (Allah) Most Gracious that He should beget a son. \nاِنْ كُلُّ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِلَّاۤ اٰتِى الرَّحْمٰنِ عَبْدًا ؕ‏(93)\nIN KULLO MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE ILLAA AAATEAA RAHMAANIR A’BDAN.\nNot one of the beings in the heavens and the earth but must come to (Allah) Most Gracious as a servant. \nلَقَدْ اَحْصٰٮهُمْ وَعَدَّهُمْ عَدًّا‏(94)\nLAQAD AAHSAAHUM WAA’ADDAHUM A’ADDAN.\nHe does take an account of them (all), and hath numbered them (all) exactly. \nوَكُلُّهُمْ اٰتِيْهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فَرْدًا‏(95)\nWAKULLUHUM AAATEEHE YAWMA QEYAAMATE FARDAN.\nAnd everyone of them will come to Him singly on the Day of Judgment. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ سَيَجْعَلُ لَهُمُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وُدًّا‏(96)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SA-YAJ-A’LUL LAHOMUL RAHMAANO WUDDAN.\nOn those who believe and work deeds of righteousness, will (Allah) Most Gracious bestow love. \nفَاِنَّمَا يَسَّرْنٰهُ بِلِسَانِكَ لِتُبَشِّرَ بِهِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ وَتُنْذِرَ بِهٖ قَوْمًا لُّدًّا‏(97)\nFA-INNAMAA YASSARNAAHO BE-LESAANEKA LETUBASSHERA BEHIL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN WATUNZERA BEHI QAWMAN LLUDDAN.\nSo have We made the (Qur'an) easy in thine own tongue, that with it thou mayest give Glad Tidings to the righteous, and warnings to people given to contention. \nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍؕ هَلْ تُحِسُّ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ اَوْ تَسْمَعُ لَهُمْ رِكْزًا‏(98)\nWA AHLAKNAL QABLAHUM MIN QARNIN HAL TUHESSU MINHUM MIN AHADIM AW TASMAU’U LAHUM REKZAN.\nBut how many (countless) generations before them have We destroyed? Canst thou find a single one of them (now) or hear (so much as) a whisper of them? ",
  "merits": "There are 99 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is written in the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan that the reward for reciting this Surah is equal to ten times the number of people present at the time of Prophets Zakariyyah (a.s.), Yahya (a.s.), Eesaa (a.s.), Moosa (a.s.), Ishaaq (a.s.), Haroon (a.s.), Ibrahim (a.s.), Ya’qoob (a.s.) and Ismaaeel (a.s.) combined.\nKeeping this Surah (written) in the house ensures protection from thieves and Allah (s.w.t.) blesses the occupants of the house. It is also narrated that before going in the presence of a tyrant ruler, if a person recites ‘Kaf-Ha-Ya-’Ain-Saad’ and closes, with each letter, one finger of his right hand, and then recites ‘Ha-Mim-‘Ain-Seen-Qaaf’ and with each letter, closes one finger of his left hand; and then he comes in the presence of the tyrant and recites ‘wa a’natil wojooho lil hayyil qayyoom wa khaaba man hamala zulma’ and then he opens his fingers, he will be protected from the evil of the tyrant."
}
